  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset ecosystem in mid-2026 is experiencing a structural paradigm shift driven by legislative progress of the CLARITY Act (H.R.3633) in the Senate. This legislation establishes clear regulatory frameworks that are unlocking native Bitcoin programmability, positioning it as a direct competitor to Ethereum's long-held EVM smart contract dominance. Simultaneously, Bitcoin institutional adoption is entering a mature phase with over 2,000 U.S. advisory firms allocating to crypto ETFs, supported by sovereign wealth and pension fund interest. To handle this influx of capital, cross-chain infrastructure is rapidly shifting away from legacy wrapped bridges to intent-based, non-custodial cross-chain swap networks (such as THORChain, deBridge, and NEAR Intents), facilitating secure, direct liquidity transfers between BTC, ETH, and other major chains.",
